 **Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
-*   **Coordinate Bounds:** Coordinates outside the AABB will be clamped or extrapolated depending on `grid_sample`'s padding mode (default is zeros, but `align_corners` affects boundary behavior) [S2, unofficial].
-*   **`invgridSize` Shape:** If `aabbSize` is a tensor of shape $[3]$, `invgridSize` will also be shape $[3]$. The normalization formula relies on broadcasting `xyz_sampled` (shape $[N, 3]$) with `invgridSize` (shape $[3]$) [S2, unofficial].
-*   **Tensor Reshaping:** The input `xyz_sampled` must be correctly reshaped to $[1, N, 1, 1, 3]$ to match `grid_sample`'s expected grid format [S1, unofficial][S2, unofficial].
+*   **Coordinate Bounds**: Points outside the `aabb` will be sampled with boundary values (clamped or padded depending on `grid_sample` mode, default is usually 'border' or 'zeros' in some contexts, but `align_corners` affects the mapping of grid edges) [S1, unofficial][S2, unofficial].
+*   **Dimensionality**: The `invgridSize` calculation involves division by `aabbSize`. If `aabbSize` is a vector $[3]$, `invgridSize` becomes a vector $[3]$. The broadcasting in the normalization formula `(xyz_sampled - self.aabb[0]) * self.invgridSize - 1` works correctly if `xyz_sampled` has shape $[..., 3]$ [S2, unofficial].
+*   **Tensor Shape**: The `alpha_volume` shape must match the expectations of the grid sampling function. Sources vary between $[1, 1, H, W, D]$ and $[1, 1, D, H, W]$ [S2, unofficial][S3, unofficial].
 
